        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "**Gestures16** activates the native iOS gesture system on iPhones with a Home button, without changing the interface much — it still feels like stock iOS."
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionLabelView",
          "text": "Features",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "bold",
          "margins": "{16, 16, 0, 16}"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "useRawFormat": true,
          "markdown": "<style>ul{margin:0;padding-left:20px;}li{line-height:1.45;margin-bottom:12px;}</style><ul><li><b>Full native gesture system</b> — swipe up to go Home, swipe and hold for the App Switcher, and swipe along the bottom edge to switch apps</li><li><b>Control Center from the top</b> — pull it down from the top-right corner, just like on Face ID iPhones</li><li><b>Modern status bar</b> — the iPhone X-style layout, with the classic style available in settings</li><li><b>Lock Screen Quick Actions</b> — Flashlight and Camera buttons right on the Lock Screen</li></ul>"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionLabelView",
          "text": "Compatibility",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "bold",
          "margins": "{16, 16, 0, 16}"
        },
        {
          "class": "DepictionMarkdownView",
          "markdown": "Supported on **iPhone 8**, **iPhone 8 Plus**, **iPhone SE (2020)** and **iPhone SE (2022)** running **iOS 16.0 – 16.7.16**."
